--TEST--
`$e->location` is written at the `throw` rather than at the `new`: one never thrown reads empty, and a rethrow moves it to the rethrow site — spec § 10
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:errors/properties-not-accessors, lang:errors/rethrowing
// The synthesized constructor leaves `location` empty and `nvs_raise` fills it
// at the `throw`, from the same site constant a record producer takes — the
// site that agrees with the `backtrace` beside it, which holds the frames the
// exception unwound out of rather than the ones that built it.
var $unthrown = new RuntimeError("never thrown");
echo "unthrown=[", $unthrown->location, "]\n";

class Relay {
    public static function go(): string {
        try {
            throw new IOError("first");
        } catch (IOError $io) {
            // Rethrowing the same object rewrites its location: it is the
            // throw that records one, and this is a second throw.
            throw $io;
        }
    }
}

try {
    echo Relay::go(), "\n";
} catch (Throwable $e) {
    echo "rethrown=", $e->location, "\n";
    echo "message=", $e->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
unthrown=[]
rethrown=case.nvs:17
message=first
